Wrote the single row for Ortiz/housing. HB2721 (2024) — her co-sponsorship and "Y" vote — matches rung 5's zoning-deregulation clause directly, but the codebook's refined preemption rule says a statewide law removing the very zoning limits a rung names is `direction-only`, not `chair-shaped` (it can't prove deregulation is "at most" what she wants). Coded all three passages `direction-only`/`in-term` (earlier-chamber record counts per V5), row BLANK `direction-only`, `rests_on` empty.
